1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,300
A table for one. In China, that's not sad anymore — it's just a way to eat.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:09,800
The 2020 census counted about 125 million one-person households.

3
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:15,000
One in four homes — up from one in seven a decade earlier.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,800
So restaurants adapted.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:23,500
The clearest sign: the one-person hotpot. Your own pot, your own broth, your own pace.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,800
No sharing, no small talk.

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:32,000
Some shops even seat a toy bear across from you, so you're never quite alone.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,300
A hotpot for one: freedom, or a little bit lonely?
